G7 nations agreed to release 100 million barrels of oil reserves to ease market tensions amid the Strait of Hormuz crisis, while Russia's pledge to withhold diesel exports until sanctions are lifted threatens to tighten global fuel supply. Geopolitical escalation risks intensified as Russia prepared thousands of missiles and drones to strike Ukrainian energy infrastructure and warned of nuclear retaliation if Kaliningrad were attacked, while an attack on a Saudi power station raised regional energy security concerns. The United States imposed new sanctions on Iranian automakers and a railway company, expanded restrictions on entities suspected of sanctions evasion, and added a 50% tariff on certain Canadian goods, further straining trade relations.